{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target Java 17+ and Spring Framework 6.0 as the baseline for the increment.",
    "Utilize Spring Data Kafka and Kafka Streams APIs to implement the changelog-backed repository and off-heap local data affinity (U1).",
    "Implement custom Kafka Streams interceptors or wrappers to handle intelligent flushing of offsets and state based on message acknowledgements (U2, U3).",
    "Integrate a lightweight CoAP library (e.g., Eclipse Californium) to implement the CoAP source module for constrained environments (U4).",
    "Leverage Spring Boot to implement the Boot-based ModuleRunner, allowing XD to run without xd-containers (U8).",
    "Integrate Hadoop security (Kerberos) libraries to run Sqoop jobs against a secured HDFS cluster (U6).",
    "Use standard Spring REST templates or WebClient to implement the Java receptor client for Diego runtime (U7)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has prior experience with Spring Framework, Kafka, and Cloud Foundry components.",
    "Existing CI/CD pipelines and testing infrastructure are available and do not require setup from scratch.",
    "The term 'XD' refers to Spring XD or a similar internal module execution environment, and the existing codebase is accessible.",
    "Necessary external systems (Kafka clusters, secured HDFS, Diego runtime) are available for integration testing.",
    "Effort estimates represent pure development work and do not include project management or deployment activities."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Kafka Changelog Spring Data Repository Integration",
      "activity_description": "Integrate with Spring Data repository backed by Kafka changelog to leverage local data affinity (off-heap) for stateful stream processing (U1).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Intelligent Offset and State Flushing",
      "activity_description": "Add support to flush offsets and state intelligently based on successful message acknowledgements from the module-producer (U2, U3).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "CoAP Source Module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a CoAP source module to consume data using a bandwidth-efficient protocol suitable for constrained embedded environments (U4).",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and Properties File Configuration",
      "activity_description": "Write documentation to guide users on configuring the properties file to represent the deployment manifest (U5).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Secured HDFS Sqoop Jobs",
      "activity_description": "Add support to run Sqoop jobs against a secured HDFS cluster to restrict access to authorized users (U6).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Java Receptor Client for Diego",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Java receptor client to interact with the Diego runtime using the Java receptor REST APIs (U7).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Boot-based ModuleRunner and Deployment Properties",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Boot-based ModuleRunner for container-managed environments to run XD without xd-containers, and complete the remaining deployment properties work (U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 37
  }
}
```

